> papa
> > gugde ku no'u la sralygu'e kujoi la razgu'e kujoi la jugygu'e kujoi la
> > kolombi,as joi la ekuador joi la xingu'e kujoi la bidgu'e kujoi la
> > madagaskar joi la mexygu'e kujoi la pervu'ui zei gugde kujoi la
> gugdecudu
> >
> > No?
>
> You're missing the "only". There's probably more than 70% that are
> local to those places, even if just 70% are local to *only* those
> places. At least that's how I understand the original.
>

  Why do I need the "only"?  1) Quantifiers in lojban specify exact numbers=
,
so I'm only talking about exactly 11 countries, and 70% of the plants.  I'm
not making any claims about the other ~200 countries or 30% of the plant
species.  2)  "diklo" already has inherent in it the concept of "localized
to", and therefore are  not outside those countries.  OTOH, if the sense of
the original is that you could pick up 70% of the world's plants by visitin=
g
those eleven countries, but not precluding the possibility that you could
find those same plants elsewhere, then I have NOT captured the right sense.


>
> (And no comma is needed in ".kolombias." Commas are never needed, but
> especially in this case since "Colombia" is three syllables in
> Spanish.)
>

  Thanks.

                --gejyspa

